  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Why it queues",
      "items": [
        "idle and done inject and submit — the agent is at its prompt",
        "blocked queues: text plus a newline would answer the pending question",
        "A pane with no agent gets the text without a newline, so it cannot execute"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The terminal decides too",
      "items": [
        "A canonical tty silently discards a line past 1024 bytes on macOS",
        "A pty master blocks on write, so one stalled agent would freeze every pane",
        "Neither is overridable by --now; forcing the write loses the message"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Why Enter is a separate write",
      "items": [
        "Bytes arriving in one read look like a paste, and the CR becomes a newline",
        "Sent on its own 120 ms later, it reads as a keypress instead",
        "Verified against Claude Code, which otherwise leaves the message unsent"
      ]
    }
  ]
